WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.126
Private RAG systems need observability because impressive demos can still return incomplete,

00:00:05.126 --> 00:00:06.802
stale, or misleading answers.

00:00:06.802 --> 00:00:12.666
Teams need to know whether retrieval finds the right sources, whether answers are grounded,

00:00:12.666 --> 00:00:17.273
whether citations are useful, and whether sensitive data is handled correctly.

00:00:17.273 --> 00:00:20.205
Evaluation should cover both retrieval and generation.

00:00:20.205 --> 00:00:24.813
Retrieval metrics may track relevant source coverage, filter behavior, ranking quality,

00:00:24.813 --> 00:00:27.326
duplicate results, no-answer outcomes, and freshness.

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:31.515
Answer review may look at groundedness, citation coverage, completeness, tone,

00:00:31.515 --> 00:00:36.122
uncertainty handling, and whether the response stays inside the approved workflow.

00:00:36.122 --> 00:00:38.635
Evaluation sets make quality more repeatable.

00:00:38.635 --> 00:00:43.243
Teams can collect representative questions, expected source references, known edge cases,

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:44.918
and workflow-specific success criteria.

00:00:44.918 --> 00:00:49.945
Running those checks before and after prompt changes, model changes, source changes,

00:00:49.945 --> 00:00:52.877
or index rebuilds helps prevent quiet regressions.

00:00:52.877 --> 00:00:54.133
Logging needs discipline.

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:57.484
Prompt and response logs can help debug quality,

00:00:57.484 --> 00:01:02.092
but they may contain confidential source material, personal data, customer information,

00:01:02.092 --> 00:01:03.767
or sensitive operational details.

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:07.537
Observability should include redaction, sampling, retention limits, access control,

00:01:07.537 --> 00:01:11.307
and privacy review rather than storing everything by default.

00:01:11.307 --> 00:01:17.171
User feedback and expert review are valuable when they are connected to a process.

00:01:17.171 --> 00:01:21.359
Feedback should help improve sources, chunking, ranking, prompts, and documentation.

00:01:21.359 --> 00:01:26.804
Quality control is continuous because private RAG changes whenever the sources, index, model,

00:01:26.804 --> 00:01:28.480
permissions, or workflow changes.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.250
Useful dashboards should separate system health from answer quality.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:37.695
Latency, errors, and job status show whether the pipeline is running, while groundedness,

00:01:37.695 --> 00:01:39.370
citation usefulness, no-answer rates,

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:43.140
and reviewer findings show whether the workflow is trustworthy.
